=== layout: title-only

# Grading and Assessment

=== layout: one-panel

# Assignments, Quizzes, and Exams

@body

- Assignments: Tasks completed outside of class
  - Aims to reinforce learning or explore new topics.
  - Assigned weekly, 5-15 points, Unlimited retakes allowed.
  - Collaboration and seeking help encouraged.
- Quizzes: Short assessments to test knowledge on recent topics.
  - Aims to quickly assess understanding of recent material.
  - 20 points, 30 min, individual.
  - Followed by a group quiz during class.
- Exams: Cumulative assessments covering course material.
  - Cumulative, mid-term/final.
  - 100 points total (50 points/75 minutes each part).
  - Completed individually.

=== layout: two-panels

# Graded vs Total Percentage

@left

- Graded percentage only includes items that have a grade
- Ignores all uncompleted assignments
- More accurate when Dr. Voss has ungraded entries in the grade book

@right

- Total percentage is all gradable items in blackboard.
- Gives you a zero score on all uncompleted assignments.
  - including assignments waiting for a grade from the professor.
- More accurate when you have unattempted blackboard assignments

=== layout: title-only

# Quiz/Exam

=== layout: one-panel

# Don’t Panic

@body

- If you experience internet troubles or non-academic distractions during a quiz/exam:
  - 1. Don’t panic
  - 2. Stop and close the quiz/exam without looking at all the questions
  - 3. Contact me immediately, preferably via Discord, but you do not need to rush
- Note: Once class begins, I no longer check my email.
- If you haven't looked at all the questions, I can reset the quiz/exam
- If you have looked at some questions, I can create a new custom quiz/exam with only the portion that you haven't seen yet.

=== layout: one-panel

# Illness Policy

@body

- Since COVID, I am trying to be more considerate of student illnesses.
- If you are sick, let me know. I will provide an extension.
- If a major event interferes (car accident, etc.), again contact me.
- Communication is always helpful.

=== layout: title-only

# Quiz

=== layout: two-panels

# Quiz System Information

@left

- 20 points total in 18-24 questions
  - 1 point for each multiple choice
  - ½ point for each choice in a matching question
- 30 minutes for the quiz
  - Back-tracking is allowed
  - random order
  - Limited calculations, not testing calculator use
  - 1½  min per question
- Final Score
  - Average of Individual and Group Scores: (14 + 20)/2 = 17 points

@right

- Individual Quiz
  - on blackboard
  - Opens &gt; 20 hours before start of class
  - due BEFORE class
- Group Quiz
  - During class over Zoom and Blackboard
  - Form groups of 3-4 students
    - may take awhile to organize break out groups
  - Group scores are curved for hard quizzes

=== layout: one-panel

# Missing Group Quizzes

@body

- Make-up quizzes will be allowed for full credit only if the student notifies the instructor BEFORE the quiz/exam
- Students missing group quizzes cannot later work in a group
  - the individual score will be averaged with the minimum 18 points (or higher) instead of a group quiz score
  - so you still get the benefit of the group score average, albeit small, even though you missed the in-class quiz.

=== layout: one-panel

# Please Volunteer Only If Plan to Work in Group

@body

- You get Group Quiz points no matter what.
  - your individual score will be averaged with the standard 18 points (sometimes higher) instead of a group quiz score
- Group Quiz is not required.
- Do not join if you do not want to actively participate.
- Let me know if you want to work with someone in particular.

=== layout: one-panel

# Group Quiz Setup

@body

- If you have not finished the individual quiz, you MUST complete it before participating in the group quiz.
- Pre-Group Quiz:
  - You have been pre-assigned into groups
  - You will be placed into breakout rooms based on these groups.
  - Select one student in your group as the Recorder.
  - The Recorder will share their screen and enter the decided upon answers for the quiz.
  - The Recorder should go into Blackboard to begin the group quiz.
  - Make sure only the Recorder starts the quiz because each quiz has unique questions.
- Begin the Group Quiz:
  - You will have 30 minutes to complete the quiz
  - The first question will ask you to enter your first names.
  - Your group can discuss answers either verbally or through the chat.
  - If you need my assistance, click the 'Ask for Help' button.
- Post-Group Quiz:
  - After you submit, you should see the correct answers along with what you submitted.
  - If your group experience was not good, please reach out to me through email or direct message.
  - Once you are finished, you are free to return to the main room or stay in the breakout room and chat or whatever.

=== layout: one-panel

# Low Quiz Grades

@body

- How can I do better in this class?
- Did you complete the relevant assignments before taking the quiz?
  - The assignments and quizzes mostly have the same questions.
- Did you retake the relevant assignments and make sure you understood the questions? Did you retake them until you had a grade you were happy with?
  - The assignments and quizzes mostly have the same questions.

